message: "If you use uwreplay-gate, please cite it as below."
title: "uwreplay-gate: offloading and freshness decisions for AUV networks on replayed sea-trial channels"
abstract: >-
  Two standard underwater acoustic frame families, a JANUS-like frequency-hopped frame and a coherent
  single-carrier frame with a decision-feedback equalizer, replayed through seven measured sea-trial channels of
  the Underwater Acoustic Channel Library on one hydrophone. The replays give per-site packet-success plateaus,
  goodput with retransmissions, and failure-run statistics, which are fed back into three published designs: a
  multi-tier offloading economy, a multi-AUV data-collection planner, and the max-age-first scheduling rule.
  uwreplay-gate holds the frames and receivers, the replay protocol, the rebuilt designs, the short-probe study,
  every result file, and tests that pin every number the paper reports.
type: software
